  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Transitional Shelter Construction and Shelter repair/upgrade in Jawzjan, Badghis and Farah Provinces</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Afghanistan is descending into the worst humanitarian crisis in the world. Amidst the backdrop of an already dire situation following 40 years of war, economic decline, price increases, and rising poverty, in 2021 the people of Afghanistan faced intensified conflict, the worst drought in 27 years, the withdrawal of international forces and then the takeover of the country by the Taliban in August. Following the record displacement of nearly 700,000 people in 2021, some 9.2 million internally displaced persons (IDPs) and returnees remain in some form of displacement and in need of support to return where possible. Through this project IOM is distributing cash for transitional shelter and shelter repair to IDPs, natural disaster affected/displaced and other vulnerable groups in Jawzjan, Badghis, and Farah provinces.</narrative>
  </description>
